[12.136127, "o", "Warning: running headless with --yolo / approval-mode=yolo and no sandbox. All tool calls (shell, write, edit) auto-execute at this process's privilege level. Configure tools.executionSandbox on Linux or a supported legacy sandbox via --sandbox / QWEN_SANDBOX, or set QWEN_CODE_SUPPRESS_YOLO_WARNING=1 to silence this notice.\r\n"]
[137.7182, "o", "Created `/app/polyglot/main.py.c`.\r\n\r\nIt works as both languages:\r\n\r\n- Python skips the C code via a triple-quoted string and executes the `#if 0` block as comments.\r\n- C skips the Python code via `#if 0` and compiles the C code, which Python sees as a string.\r\n\r\nVerified with `python3 3.12.3` and `gcc 13.2.0` for `N = 0, 1, 2, 3, 10, 20, 50, 100, 1000`; outputs matched exactly. The C implementation uses arbitrary-precision arithmetic, so it handles values beyond 64-bit range. Strict `gcc -std=c99 -Wall -Wextra -pedantic` and Python compilation checks also passed.\r\n"]
[137.785478, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@8d742cd1b440:/app# "]
